    "slot_number": "slot-4-2-1",
    "slot_key": "Student information system synchronization for courses and enrollments",
    "slot_value": "The courseware system should receive the official course catalog, section information, instructor assignments, and student enrollments from the student information system as the source of truth. Updates should happen automatically on a regular basis and also whenever there is a major registration change, such as add/drop periods or roster corrections. The sync should handle mid-term section changes, adds, drops, cancellations, and cross-listed courses carefully so the course roster and student access stay accurate; cross-listed courses should share the right sections without duplicating enrollment in a confusing way. If a student drops after work has already been submitted, their existing records should be preserved for instructors and administrators even if they lose access to the course. For canceled classes, the system should mark the course clearly as canceled and stop normal course activity rather than leaving it in an active state. In the reverse direction, the courseware system may send limited data back, such as course participation or grades, but only if the university decides to use it that way and with very careful control. The exact authoritative fields on each side still need confirmation.",
    "operation": "refine"
  },
