    "slot_key": "Enrollment-status-based access transitions during add/drop",
    "slot_value": "Waitlisted students should receive temporary access during add/drop, at least to basic course information and possibly materials if the instructor allows it; they should not have full participation rights unless actually enrolled. When a student drops the course, access should generally be removed quickly, but a short grace period may be needed if there are already-submitted assignments or pending administrative updates. Access changes should follow official enrollment status, with enough flexibility to avoid disrupting legitimate transitions. During add/drop, access should not switch abruptly in the middle of in-progress assignments or graded work if it can be avoided; a short grace period tied to the next roster sync is preferred so students do not lose access before the update is fully processed. Once the official enrollment change is confirmed, access should be limited promptly and the grace period should be only a practical transition window, not an open-ended exception. If a student drops after work has already been submitted, their existing records should be preserved for instructors and administrators even if they lose access to the course.",
